    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The only kingdom within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>, ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a>, whose king was one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a> of the King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a>.</li><li>Under Charles IV <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> became an imperial capital with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-europe">Central Europe</a>’s first university, founded in 1348.</li><li>Its Hussite reformation predated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Luther</a> by a century, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/defenestration-of-prague-1618">Defenestration of Prague</a> in 1618 began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years War</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Knights</a>’ fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konigsberg">Königsberg</a>, founded in 1255, is traditionally said to have been named in honour of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottokar-ii-of-bohemia">Ottokar II of Bohemia</a>, who had joined their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

